{#
  T-2.14 — the empty state. One component for cart, favorites, orders,
  notifications and search results.

  Usage:

    {% include 'components.ui.empty-state' with {
        icon:         'shopping-bag',
        message:      trans('pages.cart.empty_cart'),
        action_label: trans('common.elements.back_home'),
        action_href:  link('/')
    } only %}

  Parameters:
    icon           required — sicon glyph without its prefix
    message        required — one sentence, through |trans. **Never a literal.**
    title          optional heading above the message
    action_label   optional — with `action_href`, renders the way onward
    action_href    optional
    action_variant 'primary' (default) · any variant of components.ui.button
    testid         optional `data-testid`, to keep upstream's hooks working
    level          heading level for `title`, 2 by default
    class          extra classes on the card

  DERIVED UNDER B8, AND THE DERIVATION IS THAT NOTHING WAS INVENTED. No artboard
  draws an empty state. The ruling says to build one from existing components and
  upstream templates in the established visual language — warm page, white card,
  subtle border, the same buttons — so this is exactly three things the theme
  already has: T-2.15's `.card`, upstream's own `.no-content-placeholder` column,
  and T-2.05's button. **The only new CSS is the retune of upstream's two colours
  to tokens**, in 04-components/empty-state.scss.

  IT EMITS `.no-content-placeholder` DELIBERATELY. That class already appears in
  five upstream templates — cart, orders, blog, brands, brand detail. Reusing it
  means those five and this component cannot drift into two different empty
  states, and the retune reaches them without any of them being edited.

  THE COPY IS ALWAYS THE CALLER'S. Five contexts need five sentences, and each
  belongs to the page that knows its own situation — most of them already exist
  in upstream's catalogue (`pages.cart.empty_cart`, `pages.orders.non_orders`).
  This component adds no string of its own and therefore cannot put the wrong
  one on a page.

  THE ICON IS DECORATIVE, WHICH IS WHY IT PASSES NO LABEL. It restates the
  message beside it; naming it would make a screen reader say the same thing
  twice. T-2.04's partial hides it by default, and that default is correct here.
#}
<div class="card empty-state {{ class|default('') }}"
     {% if testid is defined and testid is not empty %}data-testid="{{ testid }}"{% endif %}>
    <div class="no-content-placeholder">
        <span class="icon">
            {% include 'components.ui.icon' with { name: icon, size: 'xl' } only %}
        </span>

        {% if title is defined and title is not empty %}
            <h{{ level|default(2) }} class="empty-state__title">{{ title }}</h{{ level|default(2) }}>
        {% endif %}

        <p>{{ message }}</p>

        {% if action_label is defined and action_label is not empty
              and action_href is defined and action_href is not empty %}
            {% include 'components.ui.button' with {
                label:   action_label,
                href:    action_href,
                variant: action_variant|default('primary'),
                class:   'empty-state__action'
            } only %}
        {% endif %}
    </div>
</div>
